    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> tribal confederation led by the Bayandur clan, based first at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diyarbakir">Diyarbakır</a> and from 1469 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a> it destroyed the Qara Qoyunlu and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid</a> Abu Sa’id to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</li><li>Defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1473, it split after 1490 and gave way to the Safavid state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a>’s grandson Ismail.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-i">Ismail I</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid dynasty</a> that overthrew the Aq Qoyunlu, was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a>’s grandson through his daughter by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodora-megale-komnene">Theodora Komnene</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

